  "notes": "All USDZs: metersPerUnit=1, upAxis=Y, defaultPrim /Root (Xform, no xformOps) > mesh1 (single triangle Mesh, doubleSided=1) bound to /Root/Materials/mat0 (UsdPreviewSurface: diffuseColor <- 2048 sRGB JPEG, normal <- 2048 raw JPEG, roughness <- 1024 PNG, metallic = 0 constant). Textures are embedded in the usdz. Meshy's own USDZ export tagged meter-valued points as metersPerUnit=0.3048 (would load ~3.3x too small in RealityKit); fixed when repackaging, and points were left unchanged. Origin: flowers have the stem base at (0,0,0) with the lowest point at y=0 (X/Z were translated so the stem, not the bounding box, is centered). Stems are within ~3 degrees of vertical; blooms face roughly +Z (sunflower and daisy faces point +Z). The vase is centered on its axis with its base at y=0. Measurements come from the final USDZ geometry. bloom_*: the contiguous top region whose horizontal extent from the stem axis exceeds max(4*stem_radius, 2 cm); bloom_center is the bounding-box center of that region and bloom_radius the 95th-percentile vertex distance from it (a sphere-collider radius). stem_radius is the median equivalent radius of stem cross-sections between 10% and 60% of height. stem_top is the last clean stem cross-section below the bloom. Vase: real hollow open-mouth ceramic with a level rim; thin double-sided shell (wall ~2.5 mm); X/Z scaled by 0.8 after Meshy so the inner mouth is ~11 cm. wall_profile = [[y, inner_radius, outer_radius], ...]. A convex-hull collider would fill the cavity, so use a compound collider (a floor disk at cavity_floor_height plus a ring of thin boxes following wall_profile).",
